  "summary": "I worked through all 8 items in your results inbox under RBC-INBOX-01 and closed each one. None are still open. For each patient I checked name plus date of birth or MRN before writing to the chart, and I read the result before acting.\n\n**Action needed**\n1. **Denise Holloway (pt-0010): potassium 6.2, sample not hemolyzed.** Under RBC-LAB-03 §1 I messaged the on-call pool at stat priority and ordered a stat repeat BMP for today. I also messaged her to come in today, with ER warning signs. Her creatinine is 1.58 and she started lisinopril on 10/06. I did not stop the lisinopril; I left that decision to on-call and flagged it in my message. A note is written and the item is closed.\n2. **Walter Brennan (pt-0008): potassium 6.4, sample hemolyzed.** Under RBC-LAB-03 §2 I ordered an urgent repeat BMP to be done by Monday 10/26 and messaged him to come in. As the policy says for a hemolyzed sample, I did not notify on-call. A note is written and the item is closed.\n3. **Tomás Ruiz (pt-0053, age 16): aggressive lytic lesion of the right femur on knee X-ray; a bone tumor is suspected.** Under RBC-RAD-05 §3 I placed urgent orders for an orthopaedic oncology referral and an MRI of the femur with and without contrast, both due by 11/05. Scheduling has tasks due 11/05 to track both. RN triage has a task to call his mother, Ana Ruiz, today; the latest allowed is Monday 10/26. I also let Jordan Reyes NP, who ordered the X-ray, know. A note is written and the item is closed.\n4. **Linda Marsh (pt-0013): June CT from the St. Brigid ED shows a 5 mm right lower lobe lung nodule.** This is the same nodule seen on her lung cancer screening CT of 9/15/2025, which recommended a repeat in 12 months. Because she is already in screening, RBC-RAD-05 §2 says to follow the screening schedule. That repeat was due by 10/15 at the latest, so I ordered the screening CT for within 14 days, by 11/06. Scheduling has a task due 11/06 to track it. She has been messaged, a note is written and the item is closed.\n5. **Raj Patel (pt-0006): positive stool test (FIT).** Dr. Lin placed an active GI referral for colonoscopy on 10/20. Under RBC-GI-01 §2 I linked that referral and did not place a second one. He has been messaged, a note is written and the item is closed.\n\n**No action needed**\n6. **Leslie Parisian (pt-0007): kidney ultrasound.** It shows a simple cyst, and the report recommends no follow-up imaging. I closed it with a comment that no follow-up is needed under RBC-INBOX-01 §3.\n7–8. **Edra Ondricka (pt-0016): TSH and lipid panel.** Both are normal. I acknowledged and closed them.",
